   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to permitting Congregation Gates of Prayer to file an application for certain real property tax exemptions",
    "basePrintNo": "S252",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S252-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Nassau County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S252\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act in relation to permitting Congregation Gates of Prayer to file\nan application for certain real property tax exemptions\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 420-a of the real property tax law is amended to authorize the\nCounty of Nassau to accept a retroactive application for real property\ntax exemptions from Congregation Gates of Prayer.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nCongregation Gates of Prayer is a not-for-profit tax exempt\norganization that owns property located in Nassau County. This\nproperty is used as a place of worship as well as other religious\nobservances. The property is located at 138 Hards Lane, Lawrence, New\nYork, 11559. This legislation would provide Congregation Gates of\nPrayer with an exemption from real property taxes pursuant to 420-a of\nthe Real Property Tax Law from July 1, 2014 for part of the 2013-2014\nassessment roll with respect to part of the 2014 General Tax, the full\n2014-2015 assessment roll with respect to the 2014/15 school tax and\nthe 2015 General Tax and the 2015/16 assessment roll with respect to\n2015/16 School Tax and the 2016 General Tax.\n\nThe transfer of ownership to Congregation Gates of Prayer took place\nafter the tax exempt filing date, and as a result, the organization\nwas liable for approximately twenty-four months of property taxes\ndespite their not-for-profit status. Congregation Gates of Prayer has\nfiled a timely application for tax exemption with the Nassau County\nAssessor. In order to preserve the community's organization for the\nuse by its residents, Congregation Gates of Prayer needs the requested\nrelief from real property taxes.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a New Bill\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThe specific pro-rata amount of tax refund will be calculated by the\nNassau County Assessor's Office.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
