    "lawSection": "Nassau County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S252B\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act in relation to permitting Congregation Gates\nof Prayer of Far Rockaway to file an application for certain real\nproperty tax exemptions\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nAuthorizes the County of Nassau to grant a real property tax exemption\nto the Congregation Gates of Prayer of Far Rockaway.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 420-a of the real property tax law is amended to authorize the\nCounty of Nassau to accept a retroactive application for real property\ntax exemptions from Congregation Gates of Prayer of far Rockaway.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nCongregation Gates of Prayer of Far Rockaway is a not-for-profit tax\nexempt organization that owns property located in Nassau County. This\nproperty is used as a place of worship as well as other religious\nobservances. The property is located at 138 Hards LanePP, Village of\nLawrence, New York, 11559. This legislation would provide Congregation\nGates of Prayer with an exemption from real property taxes pursuant to\n420-a of the Real Property Tax Law for the 2014-15 assessment roll\nwith respect to part of the 2014-15 school tax and the 2015 General\nTax, and the 2015-16 assessment roll with respect to 2015-16 School\nTax and the 2016 General Tax.\n\nThe transfer of ownership to Congregation Gates of Prayer of Far\nRockaway took place after the tax exempt filing date, and as a result,\nthe organization was liable for approximately twenty-four months of\nproperty taxes despite their not-for-profit status.  Congregation\nGates of Prayer of Far Rockaway has filed a timely application for tax\nexemption with the Nassau County Assessor. In order to preserve the\ncommunity's organization for the use by its residents, Congregation\nGates of Prayer of Far Rockaway needs the requested relief from real\nproperty taxes.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\n\nThe specific pro-rata amount of tax refund will be calculated by the\nNassau County Assessor's Office.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
